The branch builds AI4DEV-82 ("Window guard at the sitting boundary — park before the wall
instead of dying mid-sitting"): three hooks that enforce the founder's 85% usage-window line —
a PreToolUse gate that refuses `Agent` spawns at or over the line, a per-tool alarm that puts
the verdict line in front of any model within one tool call, and a founder-facing prompt-stamp
alarm — plus a sensor-written one-line verdict file, a shared verdict library, a drill, and two
contract amendments. The plan is `loop/items/AI4DEV-82/plan.md`; judge the code against it as
written.

The branch base is 390042c; the branch diff is everything from there to the pinned commit. The
changed code:

- `loop/work/window-lib.ps1` (new) — the one verdict implementation (`Get-WindowVerdict`,
  `Format-WindowVerdictLine`) and the one path formula (`Get-WindowDir`, `Get-WindowSnapshotPath`,
  `Get-WindowVerdictPath`)
- `loop/work/window-gauge.ps1` — now a thin CLI over the library; behaviour-neutrality is
  claimed for every existing caller
- `loop/work/window-wait.ps1`, `loop/work/window-sim.ps1` — the 85 line and its boundary cases
- `loop/work/statusline.ps1` — the sensor: writes the verdict line FIRST, then the snapshot, in
  ONE try block; the claimed invariant is that the verdict file can never be older than the
  snapshot beside it
- `loop/work/window-gate.ps1` (new) — PreToolUse on `Agent`; the deny JSON carries window,
  percent, line, reset time and the parking choreography; UNKNOWN allows with
  `additionalContext` plus `systemMessage`; internal errors fail open but never mute
- `loop/work/window-alarm.cmd` (new) — the per-tool checkpoint; findstr-anchors the verdict
  file's first token, exit 2 with the line on stderr, silence otherwise
- `loop/work/stamp-hook.ps1` — computes the verdict via the library once per prompt; PAUSE
  yields a `WINDOW ALARM` line, UNKNOWN a non-halting note
- `loop/drills/window-watchdog-drill.ps1` (new) — four assertion groups plus fault injection,
  all against synthetic snapshots behind an `AI4GOOD_WINDOW_DIR` override
- `loop/drills/run-drills.ps1` — the drill folded in, and `$failed` now computed after ALL
  asserts so a folded FAIL binds the exit code
- `.claude/settings.json` — three new hook entries (PreToolUse matcher `Agent`; PostToolUse and
  PostToolUseFailure with no matcher)
- `.claude/skills/work/shared-invariants.md` and `.claude/agents/conductor.md` — the recorded
  85-line ruling and the parking choreography

