 194:     # IT COMPUTES, IT DOES NOT READ THE ONE-LINE VERDICT FILE. The per-tool alarm reads that line
 195:     # because it is paid on every tool call; this runs once per prompt, beside several git calls,
 196:     # so the cost of computing is nothing. And it must compute: a raw read would echo an hours-old
 197:     # OK if the sensor had died, and the founder channel is exactly the one that must always apply
 198:     # the staleness rules rather than repeat a frozen answer.
