 296: # =====================  folded guards - whole scripts, folded in as one assertion  =====================
 297: #
 298: # EVERY ASSERT MUST RUN BEFORE $failed IS COMPUTED. It did not: $failed was computed here, above
 299: # the twin guard, so a twin FAIL printed, was counted in the summary line, and this script still
 300: # exited 0 - a guard that does not bind, which is the exact defect class this drill set removes.
 301: # Found by the AI4DEV-82 plan review. The fix is the ordering below, and it repairs the twin guard
 302: # at the same time.
 303: 
 304: # ---- twin guard: the orchestrator pair must be identical apart from the declared differences.
 305: # The rule drifted within a day of being relied on (2026-08-10); this assertion is that lesson.
