s step to settle it. It is only HALF true, and the half that is\nfalse is dangerous, so the measurement is recorded here before the setup that depends on it.\n\n=== docker server version ===\n29.6.2\n\n=== containers running BEFORE setup ===\nai4good-runner | Up 3 days\nsupabase_analytics_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | Up 6 hours (healthy)\nsupabase_auth_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | Up 6 hours (healthy)\nsupabase_db_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | Up 7 hours (healthy)\nsupabase_edge_runtime_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | Up 6 hours\nsupabase_inbucket_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | Up 7 hours (healthy)\nsupabase_kong_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | Up 7 hours (unhealthy)\nsupabase_pg_meta_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | Up 7 hours (healthy)\nsupabase_realtime_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | Up 6 hours (healthy)\nsupabase_rest_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | Up 7 hours\nsupabase_storage_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | Up 6 hours (healthy)\nsupabase_studio_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | Up 7 hours (healthy)\nsupabase_vector_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | Restarting (0) 24 seconds ago\n\n=== MEASURED: --workdir alone does not isolate a slot ===\nProbe A - the CLI runs FROM THE REPO (itself a Supabase project) with --workdir slot-1.\nExpected, if --workdir were sufficient: slot-1 ports and slot-1 containers.\nStopped services: [supabase_imgproxy_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu supabase_pooler_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu]\n{\"DB_URL\":\"postgresql://<redacted>@127.0.0.1:55322/postgres\",\"API_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:55321\",\"REST_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:55321/rest/v1\",\"GRAPHQL_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:55321/graphql/v1\",\"FU\n\nREAD THAT AGAIN: the URL is the slot port 55321, and the container health it reports is the\nPERSONAL project poancmeitlmxejofwzuu. One command, two projects. A db reset under this\nhybrid would name one database and rebuild another.\n\nProbe B - the same command from C:\\, which is not a Supabase project.\n{\"_tag\":\"Error\",\"error\":{\"code\":\"LegacyStatusDbInspectError\",\"message\":\"failed to inspect container health: Error response from daemon: No such container: supabase_db_ai4good-slot-1\"}}\n\nProbe B resolves the identity correctly and says so: no such container supabase_db_ai4good-slot-1.\nCONCLUSION, now built into the code: the pool always passes --workdir AND sets the working\ndirectory to the same slot. The flag says which project; the working directory stops anything\nelse from claiming to be one. The first setup attempt on this machine ran with the working\ndirectory on the repo: supabase start found the personal database container healthy, decided\nthe project was already running, and exited zero having created no slot container at all.\n\n=== the personal stack, read BEFORE setup (a read; nothing is written to it) ===\nStopped services: [supabase_imgproxy_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu supabase_pooler_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu]\n{\"DB_URL\":\"postgresql://<redacted>@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres\",\"API_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321\",\"REST_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/rest/v1\",\"GRAPHQL_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/graphql/v1\",\"FUNCTIONS_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1\",\"MCP_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/mcp\",\"STUDIO_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54323\",\"PUBLISHABLE_KEY\":\"<redacted-key>\",\"SECRET_KEY\":\"<redacted-key>\",\"JWT_SECRET\":\"<redacted>\",\"ANON_KEY\":\"<redacted-jwt>\",\"SERVICE_ROLE_KEY\":\"<redacted-jwt>\",\"MAILPIT_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54324\",\"INBUCKET_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54324\",\"STORAGE_S3_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/storage/v1/s3\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_ID\":\"<redacted>\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET\":\"<redacted>\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_REGION\":\"local\",\"message\":\"\"}\n\n=== removing the two slot directories left by the first, failed attempt ===\nslot-1 present after removal: False\nslot-2 present after removal: False\ncontainers named for a slot before setup: \n\n=== bun tests/at/harness/db-pool.ts setup ===\ndb-pool setup — pool root C:\\Users\\nirdr\\AppData\\Local\\ai4good-build\\db-slots\ndb-pool setup — source configuration C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Down