:\"ses_01541a198ffeMeZOHEAs76N82N\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me check the expected.ts refusal message and scan the committed transcripts for unredacted credentials.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1786350144471,\"end\":1786350145542}}}\r\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1786350145912,\"sessionID\":\"ses_01541a198ffeMeZOHEAs76N82N\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_feac4116c0013pHOvaE7h3wbgk\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"e097e2f952e0367d7010c2a5b335a45a3a3d5437\",\"messageID\":\"msg_feac3afea001dsk6dCgrkKp2BN\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_01541a198ffeMeZOHEAs76N82N\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":143140,\"input\":1772,\"output\":242,\"reasoning\":2758,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":138368}},\"cost\":0.0007377552}}\r\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1786350148368,\"sessionID\":\"ses_01541a198ffeMeZOHEAs76N82N\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_feac41b0d0010DltiEBqklE2mT\",\"messageID\":\"msg_feac4130b0014c1hiicQ79xxj8\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_01541a198ffeMeZOHEAs76N82N\",\"snapshot\":\"fc7e2be917afeee4c7ec338119268ccda1d8816b\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1786350169308,\"sessionID\":\"ses_01541a198ffeMeZOHEAs76N82N\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_00_JvTg7MsHz9ojj3oDB5CU0713\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\nirdr\\\\Downloads\\\\ai4good\\\\.claude\\\\worktrees\\\\agent-a064eb77d7bb37dd7\\\\loop\\\\items\\\\AI4DEV-79\\\\artifacts\\\\gate1-sol-distillate.md\",\"limit\":40},\"output\":\"<path>C:\\\\Users\\\\nirdr\\\\Downloads\\\\ai4good\\\\.claude\\\\worktrees\\\\agent-a064eb77d7bb37dd7\\\\loop\\\\items\\\\AI4DEV-79\\\\artifacts\\\\gate1-sol-distillate.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: SOURCE   loop/items/AI4DEV-79/artifacts/gate1-sol-output.md\\n2: REVIEWER gpt-5.6-sol, reasoning effort xhigh, sandbox read-only (codex CLI 0.146.0, session id 019fe865-7f42-76d0-a39c-fbb5221a7f75)\\n3: COUNT    15 findings in source → 15 extracted\\n4: NOTES    Declared count line \\\"PLAN REVIEW: 15 FINDINGS\\\" matches the extracted count. Severity scale as stated by the reviewer: high = isolation/data-safety violation or a false completion gate; medium = supported states or required proof are missing; low = a factual error that weakens evidence.\\n5: \\n6: [1] severity: high   loop/items/AI4DEV-79/plan.md:106\\n7:     claim: \\\"File equality cannot enforce D3's invariant that the on-disk config describes the successfully restarted stack.\\\"\\n8:     why it matters: \\\"If the process stops after writing config but before a successful restart, the next occupancy sees equal text and skips restart, leaving either a stopped slot or a running stack with the previous auth behavior.\\\"\\n9:     unverified-runtime-claim: no\\n10:     raw: gate1-sol-output.md:3-6\\n11: \\n12: [2] severity: high   loop/items/AI4DEV-79/plan.md:120\\n13:     claim: \\\"D4 and D6 create separate reservation and occupancy files instead of the ruled single per-slot claim transitioning between reserved and occupied states.\\\"\\n14:     why it matters: \\\"A sweep can delete the reservation while its occupancy lock remains, allowing another item to reserve the slot and then be refused; the plan also provides no ownership-checked transition preventing a delayed release from deleting a newer reservation.\\\"\\n15:     unverified-runtime-claim: no\\n16:     raw: gate1-sol-output.md:8-11\\n17: \\n18: [3] severity: high   loop/items/AI4DEV-79/plan.md:120\\n19:     claim: \\\"Reusing `acquireStackLock` permits takeover of a live occupier after `LOCK_STALE_MINUTES`, not only takeover of a dead PID.\\\"\\n20:     why it matters: \\\"`runner.ts:285-288` treats an alive holder older than 60 minutes as stale, so a second verify can take the claim and reset the first verify's database while it is still running.\\\"\\n21:     unverified-runtime-claim: no\\n22:     raw: gate1-sol-output.md:13-16\\n23: \\n24: [4] severity: high   loop/items/AI4DEV-79/plan.md:145\\n25:     claim: \\\"D8 deliberately leaves the drill tier resetting the repo-configured personal stack despite the settled requirement that this stack remain untouchable.\\\"\\n26:     why it matters: \\\"`--tier drill` still follows `runner.ts:1044-1105` and executes `db reset` against the 54321 stack; an unfiled future follow-up does not deliver the ruled protection.\\\"\\n27:     unverified-runtime-claim: no\\n28:     raw: gate1-sol-output.md:18-21\\n29: \\n30: [5] severity: high   loop/items/AI4DEV-79/plan.md:101\\n31:     claim: \\\"The identity overlay omits valid host-port fields such as `local_smtp.smtp_port` and `local_smtp.pop3_port` shown in `supabase/config.toml:110-111`.\\\"\\n32:     why it matters: \\\"Enabling them with personal defaults makes D5 reject a legitimate item config, while assigning any other common value preserves that same value in both slots and allows the slots to collide with each other.\\\"\\n33:     unverified-runtime-claim: no\\n34:     raw: gate1-sol-output.md:23-26\\n35: \\n36: [6] severity: high   loop/items/AI4DEV-79/plan.md:139\\n37:     claim: \\\"D7's fixed copy set is not the dependency closure of the item's regenerated config.\\\"\\n38:     why it matters: \\\"Active `schema_paths`, TLS keys, signing keys, email templates, or storage paths can point to files absent from the slot, while the plan never defines whether slot start receives the config's `env()` variables or the existing credential-dropping child environment; settle this with a fixture config containing one active relative file and one `env()` provider, followed by a restart and behavior probe.\\\"\\n39:     unverified-runtime-claim: yes\\n40:     raw: gate1-sol-output.md:28-31\\n\\n(Showing lines 1-40 of 94. Use offset=41 to continue.)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"SOURCE   loop/items/AI4DEV-79/artifacts/gate1-sol-output.md\\nREVIEWER gpt-5.6-sol, reasoning effort xhigh, sandbox read-only (codex CLI 0.146.0, session id 019fe865-7f